  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme Completion Review for the Rehabilitation of Freetown Water Supply</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A team of two consultants will be contracted to review and measure the impact of what the Freetown Water programme has demonstrated, the extent to which outputs been achieved i.e. did the activities of the programme deliver the outputs and have the outputs of the programme resulted in achieving the programme&#x2019;s outcome (purpose)? 
The programme has generally performed well scoring As or Bs in previous annual reviews, but there hasn&#x2019;t been any external evaluation during the life of the programme. We judge that FCDO will benefit from the services of an experienced external consultant to help us understand the balance between assessing project partner performance in delivering against project milestones as established in the contract (which has gone through regular renegotiations based on context, budget etc), and the initial ambition set out in the business case.</narrative>
  </description>
